{"replacements":[{"file":"harness.cjs","old":"for (const d of ['/profile','/downloads','/temp','/home','/home/AppData/Roaming','/home/AppData/Local']) await ap(OUT + d);","new":"for (const d of ['/profile','/downloads','/temp','/home','/home/Desktop','/home/Documents','/home/Downloads','/home/AppData/Roaming','/home/AppData/Local','/home/AppData/Local/Temp']) await ap(OUT + d);
  // Seed the dedicated experiment profile's native file-chooser default:
  // profile/Default/Preferences -> selectfile.last_directory = absolute OUT/downloads.
  // Merge-only write: if Preferences already exists, parse it and update only the
  // single selectfile key; all other existing keys are preserved. Nothing outside
  // the owned OUT/profile directory, no registry, no global config is touched.
  try {
    const prefDir = path.join(OUT, 'profile', 'Default');
    await ap(prefDir);
    const prefFile = path.join(prefDir, 'Preferences');
    let prefs = {};
    if (fs.existsSync(prefFile)) {
      try { prefs = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(prefFile, 'utf8')) || {}; } catch (_) { prefs = {}; }
    }
    prefs.selectfile = Object.assign({}, prefs.selectfile, { last_directory: path.join(OUT, 'downloads') });
    fs.writeFileSync(prefFile, JSON.stringify(prefs));
  } catch (_) { /* non-fatal: chooser falls back to HOME/Downloads inside OUT */ }"}],"rationale":"Two concerns, one surgical patch. (1) HOME/USERPROFILE already redirect to OUT/home in LAUNCH.env, but Windows Chrome's file chooser resolves standard user folders (Desktop/Documents/Downloads) under USERPROFILE, so those subfolders are now pre-created inside the temporary HOME (plus AppData/Local/Temp) — keeping all dialog-side temp/user paths confined to OUT without touching the launch env. (2) The brand-new, experiment-owned profile at OUT/profile gets a minimal profile/Default/Preferences seeding only selectfile.last_directory to the absolute OUT/downloads, so the native chooser opens at the isolated downloads dir on first use. The write is merge-only (reads and preserves any pre-existing Preferences keys; the profile is newly created so nothing user-owned can be overwritten) and confined to the owned profile directory — no registry, global Chrome config, dependencies, or auth files are involved. All existing launch flags, chromiumSandbox/ignoreDefaultArgs isolation, offline mode, downloadsPath, cancel oracle, and ownership checks are left byte-for-byte unchanged. Note for the executor: this seeding is only an initial hint for the chooser's starting directory; if a scenario requires the dialog to start elsewhere, native navigation (typing/choosing a path in the dialog) remains allowed as a separate explicit step. This patch has not been exercised against a live browser — no test run is claimed; verification happens when the step11-visible-04 execution copy is launched."}
